{
  "id": "ep086",
  "duration": 57.364,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.85,
      "text": "A zombie star survived its own supernova explosion.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of a double-detonation supernova (eso2511c).tiff",
        "credit": "ESO/M. Kornmesser",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_a_double-detonation_supernova_(eso2511c).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.067,
          "end": 3.867,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.85,
      "end": 9.445,
      "text": "Normally, these powerful runaway blasts completely obliterate a dying white dwarf star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of the initial shape of a supernova explosion (eso2520a).jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/L. Cal\u00e7ada",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_the_initial_shape_of_a_supernova_explosion_(eso2520a).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.867,
          "end": 6.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 6.367,
          "end": 9.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.445,
      "end": 16.115,
      "text": "But in the year 1181, astronomers witnessed a strange, rare cosmic blast in the night sky.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "SN 1181 - Schaefer 2023 Figure 5.png",
        "credit": "Bradley E. Schaefer",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SN_1181_-_Schaefer_2023_Figure_5.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.433,
          "end": 16.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 16.115,
      "end": 23.21,
      "text": "At the center of its remnant, IRAS 00500+6713, a bizarre zombie star survived.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Tycho-supernova-xray.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/CXC/Rutgers/J.Warren & J.Hughes et al.",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tycho-supernova-xray.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.1,
          "end": 19.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.667,
          "end": 23.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.21,
      "end": 30.03,
      "text": "X-ray data from the XMM-Newton telescope recently revealed the trick behind this stellar miracle.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "XMM-Newton spacecraft animations (SVS20399 - XMM Beauty Still).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio - NASA/ESA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XMM-Newton_spacecraft_animations_(SVS20399_-_XMM_Beauty_Still).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.2,
          "end": 26.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 26.6,
          "end": 30.033,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.03,
      "end": 35.125,
      "text": "A carbon-oxygen white dwarf crashed directly into an oxygen-neon white dwarf.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Still Illustrations of White Dwarf Gravitational Wave Merger (2005-j0806-more-2 - wd 03).tiff",
        "credit": "(Credit: GSFC/D.Berry)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Still_Illustrations_of_White_Dwarf_Gravitational_Wave_Merger_(2005-j0806-more-2_-_wd_03).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.033,
          "end": 31.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 31.967,
          "end": 35.133,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.125,
      "end": 42.025,
      "text": "This intense collision triggered a partial Type [Iax](/w\u02c8\u028cn\u02c8I\u02c8\u025bks/) supernova instead of a total explosion.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.133,
          "end": 42.033,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.025,
      "end": 52.645,
      "text": "Today, the surviving star WD J005311 continues screaming through space, blowing an intense stellar wind of carbon-burning ashes.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA-JAXA XRISM Mission Sees Pulsar Accreting Companion's 'Wind' (SVS15099 - Still2).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio - NASA\u2019s Goddard Space Flight Center Conceptual Image LaboratoryAlt text: Animation of the BP Crucis system0:00 A wide view, showing the giant star, its gas stre",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA-JAXA_XRISM_Mission_Sees_Pulsar_Accreting_Companion%27s_%27Wind%27_(SVS15099_-_Still2).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.033,
          "end": 47.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 47.333,
          "end": 52.633,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 52.645,
      "end": 57.014,
      "text": "This chaotic remnant proves that a star can actually outlive its own doom.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of a double-detonation supernova (eso2511c).tiff",
        "credit": "ESO/M. Kornmesser",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_a_double-detonation_supernova_(eso2511c).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 52.633,
